[06:28] e3fb62ebfa4f36acf5cbff6a6ed0f2e0: it's just that we do have implementations and several updates to the spec without any kind of review :)
[06:28] e3fb62ebfa4f36acf5cbff6a6ed0f2e0: though maybe that's not too different from HTML5
[08:38] e3fb62ebfa4f36acf5cbff6a6ed0f2e0: a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2, btw, you're violating several SHOULD-level requirements by doing so
