[15:58] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: Have been using vim as the only i use for about 6 months now, tres pleased.  One thing I am stuck on is how do I close a single buffer?
[16:00] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: ATM I have F5/6 mapped to next and prev bufferes and I want to be able to skip ones, I assume by closing it. As currently I find I have to close vim and reopen only the ones I want
[16:01] bbfe187fc48d9171af3b60d269c8b407: km0ti0n: :bdel
[16:04] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: ooo, fantastic... Thanks
[16:04] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: That's great I'll never have to close vim again!
[16:06] bbfe187fc48d9171af3b60d269c8b407: km0ti0n: there is another great option - if you use :set hidden you'll be able to switch between the buffers without having to save the chages.
[16:09] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: Oh yeah, I use that already.
[16:11] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: that's a god send, but without :bdel it gets a bit hairy knowing what's open and edited.
[16:12] bbfe187fc48d9171af3b60d269c8b407: km0ti0n: :help buffers will give you a lot of information how to deal with buffers.
[16:12] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: damn, I was searching for :h close should have thought about that
[16:13] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: Thakns for your help. :D
[16:14] bbfe187fc48d9171af3b60d269c8b407: km0ti0n: you're welcome
[16:14] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: I noticed that Vim 7 has tabbed interface now.  Have you used it?
[16:15] bbfe187fc48d9171af3b60d269c8b407: not yet
[16:15] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: <a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/diwaker/105994000/">http://www.flickr.com/photos/diwaker/105994000/</a>
[16:15] bbfe187fc48d9171af3b60d269c8b407: I'm still using vim6
[16:19] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: hum,m, not my cuppa tea ATM I think.
[16:22] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: oh, looks good
[16:23] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: I'm using vim 7.1.1
[16:23] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: I'm using vim 7.1.1
[16:23] 4068a957c5d2943fb6c7212fd4867ce1: I'm using vim 7.1.1
