CONVERSATION:
[09:56] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: hsivonen: when you have time, I wanted to ask about updating the v.nu MathML schema
[10:04] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I see that MathML 3.0 is now at CR
[10:05] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: and that the spec includes an RNC schema
[10:05] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: so...
[10:06] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: maybe it'd make sense to replace the current v.nu MathML 2.0 schema with that one
[10:07] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: and of course note in the UI that it's now doing MathML 3.0 validation
[10:07] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: after looking through the current (2.0) schema, I suspect there might be quite a few bugs in it
[10:09] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I fixed a few today, but based on that sample, I reckon there are probably more waiting to be found
[10:11] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: and it seems like that schema has not had any maintenance in a very long time
[10:11] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: upstream, I mean
[10:11] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: http://yupotan.sppd.ne.jp/relax-ng/mml2.html shows the last update was two years ago
[10:12] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: Does MathML 3.0 have any UA support?
[10:13] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: It sems dangerous to validate something that doesn't actually work in browsers
[10:13] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: yeah, true
[10:13] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: wonders what is new in MML 3.0
[10:13] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I just don't relish the prospect of making further updates to this old and buggy 2.0 schema we currently have
[10:15] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: http://www.w3.org/TR/MathML3/appendixf.html#changes.mathml2.0e-3.0
[10:15] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: (if you're interested)
[10:15] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I think the changes are pretty significant
[10:15] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I think the changes are pretty significant
[10:15] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a")
