CONVERSATION:
[10:42] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: is pretty sure you can't solve a theroem
[10:46] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Is it not reasonable to say that e.g. Fermat's Last Theorem has been solved?
[11:08] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: I guess that is common although I think it is inaccurate (should be Fermat's Last Theroem has been proven or something). However I'm the example in the spec that talks about &quot;Solving Pythagoras' theorem&quot; to mean &quot;solving for the third side of a triangle given the other two sides&quot; seems more wrong
[11:10] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: supposes it should have been called Fermat's Last Hypothesis
[11:14] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: The spec says it's 'solving for some variable', which seems a different meaning to simply 'solving'
[11:20] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (It seems probably clear enough that it means it's taking an equational form of Pythagoras' Theorem and solving that equation in terms of some variable, which is what it's doing)
[16:57] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: OK, this has been bothering me all day. In the conetxt of 11338
[16:58] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: +bug
[16:58] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: who or what is &quot;Zeros&quot;
[16:58] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: A person on #html-wg
[16:58] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: Oh
[16:58] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: I guess if I didn't habitually ignore that channel I could have saved myself a bunch of bother
[16:59] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: The bug now says &quot;Zeros = Elliott from the HTML WG&quot; too
[15:15] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (Or maybe I should fix my OCaml tokeniser generator, and then generate an html5lib-compatible tokeniser, so it's easier to attempt fancier optimisations like inlining stuff to avoid function calls)
[15:25] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: How will you do readahead one token at a time?
[15:26] b25b6b77a0087ff8385941e5545d32ea: s/token/character/
