CONVERSATION:
[17:26] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf, should prolly say that while aDoneCallback is running you cannot invoke ModificationBatch methods
[17:27] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: why?
[17:28] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf, what would happen?
[17:28] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: the &quot;batch&quot; would listen for some new modifications
[17:29] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: I guess that could work
[17:29] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: also, why not have specialized Modification interfaces?
[17:30] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: for simplicity
[17:30] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: for text / children / attributes
[17:30] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: and Modification interface is kind of based on current MutationEvent
[17:31] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: I noticed that
[17:34] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: can you see something terribly bad in the approach ?
[17:34] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: it is quite close to other proposals, of course
[17:37] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: the only thing I think is a little weird is that ModificationBatch is also the argument passed to the callback
[17:37] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: what is the 'this' of the callback?
[17:37] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: and what does .modifications return while not in a callback?
[17:38] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: I thought I said that .modifications is empty while not in callback
[17:38] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: empty list
[17:38] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: ah yeah, the comment says so
[17:39] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: the callback needs to get some parameter so that { handleBatch: function(b) {}} can be used
[17:39] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: what is the 'this' of the callback?
[17:39] 6b57ea7f33069df5914663ba9e59afdf: edb259c0e0038f3")
