[14:24] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: I am typing iwconfig wlan0 key s:&lt;the key number&gt;
[14:24] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: or even without s: same error
[14:26] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: what about iwconfig wlan0 enc s:&lt;key in ascii&gt;?
[14:26] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: same error
[14:27] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: looks like some driver's missing?
[14:27] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: did you notice I wrote &quot;enc&quot; instead of key?
[14:27] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: yes
[14:27] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: tried writing it in hex?
[14:28] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: i don't know how to transform into HEX
[14:28] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: writing it in hex is the only guaranteed way to enter the key with WEP
[14:29] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: on the linksys router it generated 4 keys out of my password
[14:29] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: now i tried to enter one of those keys
[14:30] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: well the key only contains numbers from 0-9 and letters A-F
[14:31] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: that is hex
[14:32] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: what if you set a bogus key like iwconfig wlan0 key 001122334455?
[14:33] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: then i get this same error
[14:33] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: could be the driver was compiled without WEP support. sounds unlikely though
[14:34] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: I dont recall, but you might get some info on what the driver supports when you try to set the key
[14:34] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665f1e46e: I dont know what the driver supports
[14:34] 77ac309c0e78ae7e7321bba06c1bebab: I dont know what the driver supports
[14:34] 5c495455238fa39be6c688d665")
