CONVERSATION:
[14:42] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: if/when you have time to try a few test cases, I made a patch for http://bugzilla.validator.nu/show_bug.cgi?id=689
[14:42] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: see my comment there
[14:44] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: it reports the name and line-column number of only the bottommost unclosed element, and reports it using an error-level message
[14:45] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: the current htmlparser code doesn't itself have a means for reporting info-level messages
[14:46] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: so short of adding considerably more code for handling info-level messages, the only other alternative to reporting it as an error would be to make it a warning instead
[14:47] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: anyway, it is available now at http://www.w3.org/html/check for testing
[14:48] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: for &lt;body&gt;
[14:48] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: &lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
[14:48] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: &lt;/body&gt; it highlights the &lt;p&gt;
[14:48] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: shouldn't it highlight the &lt;div&gt;?
[14:48] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: lemme check
[14:50] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: hmm, yeah
[14:51] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I'll need to fix that
[12:01] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: thanks for the latest set of xml-stylesheet test cases
[12:02] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I think I've now got handling for all those behaving as expected
[12:02] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: when you have time, please test and let me know
[12:02] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: i'm going through the previous test cases now to make sure the latest changes didn't introduce any regressions
[12:03] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: oops
[12:03] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: I'll have a look at the test cases
[12:03] a9b326df4e6da61c5b6f5e1058be83a2: cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: thanks for the test cases
[12:03] a9b326")
