conv_id=422 | raw="
CONVERSATION:
[07:00] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: http://www.smashingmagazine.com/2010/05/18/the-beauty-of-typography-writing-systems-and-calligraphy-of-the-world/ is a pretty impressive article
[07:01] 587bf8b858e15d03428e1415c33c38ef: this whitespace-in-the-grammar stuff is driving me bananas. I think the full grammar in the appendix doesn't generate this trivial stylesheet: e { ]
[07:01] 587bf8b858e15d03428e1415c33c38ef: er... rather: e { }
[07:02] 587bf8b858e15d03428e1415c33c38ef: there's no S between selector and { in ruleset, and no S at the end of selector
[07:02] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: I think the grammar generally works so that most productions have trailing whitespace, so that you don't need additional whitespace after a production
[07:02] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: but there have certainly been errors
[07:03] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: which grammar are you looking at, anyway?
[07:03] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: There are too many.
[07:03] 587bf8b858e15d03428e1415c33c38ef: http://www.w3.org/TR/CSS2/grammar.html
[07:03] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: ugh
[07:03] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: probably the least accurate one :-P
[07:04] 587bf8b858e15d03428e1415c33c38ef: has the WG published anything newer/better?
[07:04] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: no
[07:04] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: it's just that the interaction of the chapter 4 grammar and the appendix G grammar isn't particularly defined
[07:04] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: and my opinion is that the appendix G grammar doesn't really have a normative role
[07:04] 587bf8b858e15d03428e1415c33c38ef: the chapter 4 grammar is almost entirely worthless
[07:04] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: except in so far as other features in the spec neglect to mention anything about parsing
[07:05] 587bf8b858e15d03428e1415c33c38ef: except... exactly
[07:05] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: and the normative parts are mainly the chapter 4 grammar and the prose
[07:05] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: It looks to me like the selector production is the only one that's not a valid production
[07:05] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: I think the chapter 4 grammar is the only one that's not a valid production
[07:05] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: I think the chapter 4 grammar is the only one that's not a valid production
[07:05] 1")
