conv_id=435 | raw="
CONVERSATION:
[23:09] 81ca6fc846169402ae7f260a08af00e0: Sorry for the really dumb question, but what is the proper way to use the /usr/local/bin/(c)oraenv and dbhome scripts?  I keep getting syntax errors when running them.  I thought these were the scripts I use to prepare my environment to start my DB.
[23:14] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: blizzow: . oraenv (sh/bash) and source coraenv (csh)
[23:16] 81ca6fc846169402ae7f260a08af00e0: hali: Are those the only scripts I have to run before running sqlplus, logging in and starting the db?
[23:17] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: usually yes
[23:17] 81ca6fc846169402ae7f260a08af00e0: Thanks!
[23:17] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: and you just run one of them
[23:17] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: i usually do that from my login env though
[23:17] 81ca6fc846169402ae7f260a08af00e0: oh really...ok.  .oraenv it is.
[23:17] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: all they do is to set ORACLE_HOME, ORACLE_SID and add $ORACLE_HOME/bin to your PATH
[23:18] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: add those three to your bash env.. either ~/.bashrc or /etc/profile.d/orale.sh (to make it system wide)
[23:18] 81ca6fc846169402ae7f260a08af00e0: Oh, another dumb question...how hard is it to run two instances side-by-side?  I installed Oracle 9i and 10g on the same machine...is it possible to run them at the same time?
[23:18] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: yes, no problem
[23:19] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: if you look in /etc/oraenv each instance is associated with it's own ORACLE_HOME
[23:19] 81ca6fc846169402ae7f260a08af00e0: Would I have to mess with port assignments at all?
[23:19] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: soryr, /etc/oratab
[23:19] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: nope!
[23:19] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: oracle has a stand alone listener, all instances bind to the same port
[23:19] 81ca6fc846169402ae7f260a08af00e0: Sweet.  Thanks for the info.  This could be the best IRC help I've ever received.  Most people say RTFM.
[23:20] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: I'm glad to hear that.  I'm going to try to get a few more people to help me out.
[23:20] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29e8df98b1: I'll try to get a few more people to help me out.
[23:20] 443a9547033ec9d695ae9d29")
