CONVERSATION:
[23:46] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: should css3-background reference some version of HTML?
[23:47] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: or should HTML5 define the propagating behavior?
[23:59] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: Neither, I hope.
[00:06] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: my thinking was that you need a reference for stuff like &quot;XHTML html element&quot; and all
[00:07] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: I mean, everyone with half a brain knows what you mean, because most people reading that draft know a bit of HTML and XHTML and all
[00:07] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: but technically it just seems wrong
[00:13] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: Ah, yes, a bibliographic reference. I thought you meant that the propagation should only hold for HTML5, not for earlier or later versions.
[00:15] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: Isn't HTML a word in the English dictionary yet? :-)
[00:15] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: I'll a citation or two.
[19:56] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65, hmm, I don't like it that you edit my drafts afterwards and remove e.g. Latest Editor's draft
[19:56] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65, you could at least inform me
[19:56] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: That's just the pubrules.
[19:57] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: no it's not
[19:57] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: pubrules allow custom lines there
[19:57] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: see e.g. html5 or html5-diff
[19:57] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: or cors
[19:57] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: or xmlhttprequest2
[19:57] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: I tried and it complained. Otherwise I would not have bothered.
[19:58] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: hmm
[19:58] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: But I actually agree with pubrules there. There should not be a link to volatile resources there if not strictly necessary.
[19:58] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: I think I agree with you. I think it's a good idea to have a link to volatile resources, but I don't think it should be a link to volatile resources.
[19:58] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: I think it's a good idea to have a link to volatile resources, but I don't")
