conv_id=583 | raw="
CONVERSATION:
[00:10] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774, Boris had some good comments
[00:11] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: he sure did
[00:11] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: What is your take on the SVG dependency question he raised http://www.w3.org/mid/<email/>
[00:12] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: He suggested that widget engines support SVG full. Make SVG tiny an authoring requirement. I think it's a good idea. I was going to discuss it with Shapazu and Heycam. Make sure everything is ok.
[00:13] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: sounds good. I think we already had an action to ping SVG WG but they were not on our list of explicit reviewers :-(
[00:13] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: mea culpa :-(
[00:14] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: Is there any need to discuss the issue he raised re parsing non-negative integers or have you updated the spec on that comment?
[00:14] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: no probs, let me fix up the spec first to see what Boris says. He seems quite knowledgeable about SVG
[00:15] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: he had an issue that I had not identified every form of whitespace. I have added the following to the spec to address his issue: &quot;In result, excluding any U+0020 SPACE characters, convert any sequence of one or more characters marked with the [Unicode] property &quot;White_Space&quot; into a single U+0020 SPACE.&quot;
[00:16] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: is a bit surprised some Recommendation doesn't already cover WS handling ...
[00:17] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: it's a tricky thing. In some cases you want WS (e.g., license element) and in others you don't (e.g., name element).
[00:18] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: However, I have this gut feeling that we should be silent on this whole WS thing and leave it as an implementation detail
[00:19] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: I.e., how the data inside the elements in the configuration document is displayed to the end-user should be left to implementers
[00:19] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: In your dialogue with Boris, did I read that an off-the-shelf ZIP program (e.g. the zip utility on OSX) will not work with this spec?
[00:20] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: This is a general problem with Zip. It will work, so long as the filenames and the OS use the same encoding.
[00:20] c5e3539121c4944f2bbe097b425ee774: Please see my rant:  http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xml-exc-c14n#XML-ENCODING
[00:21] 4dd217ba7542bb00a127f682e2c3ad27: I think it's a good idea to have a discussion on this. I think it's a good idea to have a discussion on this. I think it's a good idea to have a discussion on this. I think it's a good idea to have a discussion on this. I think it's a good idea to have")
