conv_id=685 | raw="
CONVERSATION:
[15:19] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: hi there!
[15:19] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: I have a question about compound microformats and RDF
[15:19] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: I'm building a proof of concept where I need to convert microformats to RDF
[15:20] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: this works with the different transformations available (for example http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/glean-hcal.xsl) and with GRDDL
[15:21] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: so now I have a page with some events on this, all represented as a hCalendar event with a hCard embedded in it for address information
[15:21] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: see: http://marco.mp3-tunes.nl/microformats.html
[15:22] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: but when converting this page to RDF(http://transformr.co.uk/grddl/http://marco.mp3-tunes.nl/microformats.html), there seems to be no relation between the Vcalendar and the VCard, so with multiple events I can't figure out which VCard relates to which Vcalendar
[15:22] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: any clue on how to fix this?
[15:31] 5c326ebb67c2d98f03092fd084fd61a0: The location is marked up as a string, adr or hCard object. All uf parsers should work with the string. Some will parse adr or hCard as part of the hCalendar. Operator for example parses the adr element of your hCard
[15:34] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: but Operator does not parse the events
[15:35] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: well, i'm going to toy around a little bit with the stylesheets provided at http://esw.w3.org/topic/CustomRdfDialects
[15:35] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: in general they seem to have issues with compound microformats
[15:40] 5c326ebb67c2d98f03092fd084fd61a0: If you look at the debug mode of Operator's output you will see the hCard element inside the event. Its only saying invalid because the dtstart is a &lt;div&gt; not a &lt;abbr&gt;
[15:42] 5c326ebb67c2d98f03092fd084fd61a0: It must be down to the parser not reading the hCard as apart of the hCalandar location.
[15:56] 1f76452114ce95267e09ea331d38ab9c: it seems like RDF Calendar (http://www.w3.org/TR/rdfcal/) doesn't even support embedding a VCard to express the location of an event
[16:02] 5c326ebb67c2d98f03092fd084fd61a0: Both are based on iCalendar which has location as a string. The use of hCard came from real world uf authoring use and the hCard is a more convenient way to embed the location of an event
[16:02] 5c326ebb67c2d98f03092fd084fd61a0: I'm not sure if this is a bug or a feature. I'm not sure if the hCard is a better way to embed the location of an event than the VCard
[16:02] 5c326ebb67c2d98f03092fd084fd61a0: I")
