[06:46] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: howdy canvasers
[06:48] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: so, can anyone answer if it is per spec/functionality that if i stroke a line in a canvas, it does not clear if if reset the canvas via changing the width or clearRect()?
[06:49] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: how do you mean?
[06:49] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: do you have a sample page showing the problem?
[06:49] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: not on a reachable server.
[06:50] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: it's simple to replicate.  start with an empty canvas.  draw a line down the center.  do a clearRect() on the canvas.  the line stays
[06:51] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: curious if i'm missing a step
[06:53] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: what arguments are you passing clearRect()?
[06:56] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: 0,0,CANVASWIDTH,CANVASHEIGHT
[06:56] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: it's working for any canvas i draw actual shapes on (rects, arcs, etc)
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: so like:
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: c.beginPath();
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: c.moveTo(100,100);
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: c.lineTo(200,300);
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: c.stroke();
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: c.clearRect(0, 0, 640, 480);
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: ...doesn't work?
[06:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: (where c is the context of course)
[06:58] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: aha... is beginPath required?
[06:58] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: unless you do beginPath(), you're just adding to the last line each time
[06:58] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: stroke() doesn't reset the path
[06:59] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: so, if you stroke a line, it doesn't clear the canvas?
[06:59] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: no, it clears the canvas
[06:59] f0cd7d84a0e28adce680a953c3d2cbeb: so, if you stroke a line, it doesn")
