[19:23] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (though for &lt;a href=&quot;...&amp;copy=...&quot;&gt; it should suggest the other way around)
[19:25] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (Well, technically, the bug is only talking about URL attributes, so the brokenness of plain-text &quot;... &amp;copy ...&quot; is not relevant, but I still think it's a brokenness :-p )
[19:29] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Also it seems misleading for it to sound so sure about &quot;Error: &amp; should have been escaped as &amp;amp;.&quot; (not saying anything vague like &quot;Probable cause&quot;) when I write e.g. &quot;... &amp;lamba; ...&quot; and the real error is not the failure to escape &amp;
