CONVERSATION:
[09:29] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: I keep wishing that support for conversations via MessageChannel was more built-in
[09:30] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: how do you mean?
[09:30] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: like, when you get a message, you always get an object you can reply to the sender with. like it is built into the api.
[09:31] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: It's just a little thing, but I was wondering if you could think of some way to make it work.
[09:31] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: I keep wanting the sender to be able to do:
[09:31] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: var port = worker(or iframe).sendMessage(&quot;foo&quot;);
[09:31] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: and then the port represents the conversation
[09:32] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: and on the other side, the worker (or iframe) could do globalObject.addEventListener(&quot;message&quot;, function(e) { e.port.sendMessage(&quot;reply&quot;) }, false)
[09:32] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: a port _is_ a conversation
[09:32] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: right, i know
[09:32] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: if you want to split the conversation off, just send a port with the message
[09:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and use that port for the subconversation
[09:33] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: i know, it seems slightly less elegant for some reason to send the port as an argument
[09:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: i don't understand you example fragments
[09:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: your
[09:33] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: one second
[09:41] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: k, here is how it works now:
[09:41] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: var channel = new MessageChannel();
[09:41] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: var worker = createWorker(&quot;foo.js&quot;);
[09:41] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: var port = worker.postMessage(&quot;foo&quot;);
[09:41] 7d8a20281bb41e05c504c371880f1d08: and then the worker will send a message to the port
[09:41] 7d8a20281bb41e05c50")
