[12:56] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: nice, FF3 gets it right :-)
[12:56] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: it does?
[12:56] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: it did a second ago, not now
[12:56] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: i just get 0%
[12:56] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: oh you probably tested it before i switched it back to document
[12:56] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: yeah
[12:57] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: the reference rendering should be pixel-perfect, including font rasterisation
[12:58] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: but really the reference rendering is a test on to its own
[12:58] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: Opera 9 is doing surprisingly poorly
[12:59] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: opera 9 is hitting two bugs that i know of
[12:59] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: one, it's getting screwed by not having a &lt;head&gt; in the DOM, because one of the selectors goes through the &lt;head&gt;
[12:59] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and two, it doesn't seem to do :root
[13:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: throws in some :first-child/:last-child tests
[13:01] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: which selector goes through head?
[13:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: *:first-child + * &gt; * &gt; p
[13:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: that's equivalent to head + body &gt; div &gt; p
[13:01] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: so it's not a head selector
[13:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: it's a body selector
[13:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: so it's not a head selector
[13:01] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a79")
