CONVERSATION:
[04:53] b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: if anyone has an example of a page which ends up needing to be reparsed because of html5's charset algorithm when a meta tag is encountered, I'd very much appreciate a pointer to it
[05:11] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: &lt;script&gt;alert('A');&lt;/script&gt;&lt;!-- xx megabytes xx --&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;C&quot;&gt;
[05:11] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: where A is a byte that is interpreted differently in two encodings
[05:11] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and C is the one of those encodings that isn't hte one the browser picks by default
[05:11] b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: ah, I get you.  I thought it might be mostly to do with scripting
[05:11] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: doesn't have to be scripting
[05:11] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: could be: A&lt;!-- xx megabytes xx --&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;C&quot;&gt;
[05:12] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: it's just more obvious with an alert() because then you get to see that it shows up twice
[05:12] b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: right!  got you, thanks
[05:12] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: np
[05:13] b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: there is a web browser equipped with the HTML5 parsing algorithm now, though it's not got scripting so isn't the most useful browser for testing all the bits that require scripting :)
[05:13] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: :-)
[05:13] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: is scripting on the agenda?
[05:14] b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: at some point in the future, I believe, but nothing very soon
[05:14] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: k
[05:14] b07211a0c7cb119232799d2119cea90f: otoh, I expect there'll be useful feedback from users of NetSurf when pages break
[02:38] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: heycam: regarding the style sheet, i really don't want to go there. historically, we've had problems whenever specs don't stick closely to the official style sheet (e.g. CSS1's marble background). It also dilutes the W3C's standards, which is a problem for us. I think we should just stick to the official style sheet, and let the browser decide what to do with it.
[02:38] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: I think we should stick to the official style sheet, and let the browser decide what to do with it.
[02:38] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a")
