[19:25] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Hmm, my &lt;canvas&gt; tests have found a bug in a pre-XPSP2 Win32 string processing function, which was somewhat unexpected and irritating since it's wasted half a day - but tests are meant to find bugs, so I suppose I shouldn't complain...
[19:28] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: perhaps you should document it somewhere so others don't waste half a day too
[19:30] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: I'll complain to Microsoft that their documentation is wrong (since it looks like they updated it to account for the bug, but incorrectly), and get Mozilla's code fixed to work around it, and then I'll be happy :-)
[19:31] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: ok
[19:31] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: something opera would have to work around too?
[19:35] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Only if they use Uniscribe's ScriptItemize function (and expect it to stay within the buffer length it's given) - as far as I can tell from Opera.dll, they don't use that function, so it shouldn't be a problem
[18:44] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: http://philip.html5.org/demos/canvas/opera-3d/textured-cube.html has a totally exciting cube demo
[18:49] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: apart from the 3d snake game, all demos are a rotating cube, it seems :)
[18:50] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: I'm not really sure what else you could do with it :-p
[18:50] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: heh
[18:51] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: As far as I can tell, it can't do anything like http://canvex.lazyilluminati.com/misc/3d.html since there's no lighting
[18:52] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: and the addVertex(...) API doesn't scale very well when vertexes have coordinates, optionally texture coordinates, optionally normals, and optionally whatever else is added later
[21:08] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: try this. check the &quot;XHTML&quot; button in http://www.google.com/preferences
[21:08] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: then load the front page
[21:10] cc097e0d7183ae8436e7df709553c8c0: hmm, that option is only available if you use opera it seems
[21:10] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Is it fair to call them bozos if they're not actually generating XML incorrectly, but are just transmitting HTML incorrectly?
[21:12] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm not sure what you mean by "incorrectly" - I'm")
