[14:07] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: really doesn't like when online purchase systems show a payment page with an iframe containing (what claims to be) a page from his bank asking for his number and password for confirmation
[14:08] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: since I can't tell where the page is actually from, and even when I can tell I just find it's www.securesite.co.uk and can't tell how legitimate that is
[14:09] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (I'm not even sure if there's an easy way to tell that it's HTTPS)
[14:11] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: the banking system in the Netherlands uses redirects for that
[14:12] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Oh, actually, securesite.co.uk is something totally unrelated - the legitimate one is securesuite.co.uk
[14:14] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (http://ambrand.com/2006/09/06/is-securesuitecouk-a-phishing-scam/ etc)
[15:54] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: lol
[15:54] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: tr &gt; tbody &gt; td
[15:54] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: tbody is not implied!
[16:07] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Shouldn't that be &quot;tbody &gt; tr &gt; td&quot;?
[16:07] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: yeah
[16:09] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Ah
[18:04] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Hooray, now my parser does &lt;title&gt; and implies &lt;html&gt; and &lt;head&gt; and &lt;body&gt; etc, and I think it might even do that correctly
[18:05] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: we should change handling of &lt;title&gt; and &lt;/head&gt; in HTML5 though
[18:05] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: If that can be done by copying-and-pasting text from other sections, then I'll be happy since I won't have to do anything
[18:07] edb259c0e0038f38bb200bc20c8cbf7e: i guess it comes down to &lt;/head&gt; being ignored but only being a parse error sometimes and &lt;title&gt; being treated like a normal element except for its content model
[18:30] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: wishes he could use the tree construction tests without first having to work out how to glue his tokeniser and tree-constructor together
[18:32] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: ...and fortunately I can't see any problems with that
[18:32] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: I'm not sure if it's a bug or a feature, but I'm not sure if it's a bug or a feature
[18:33] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: I'm not sure if it's a bug or a feature, but I'm not sure if it's")
