[20:14] f4bfe7806ad6735f1dab2f9222fc539e: Hey! The HTML5 elements video, audio and canvas are inline elements, right? Or are they supposed to be inline-block? FX 5 and Chrome say &quot;inline&quot; in the CSS panel.
[20:31] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: i don't think they are intrinsically inline or block, the spec I see says it falls into both the flow content and phrasing content categories: http://www.whatwg.org/specs/web-apps/current-work/multipage/the-canvas-element.html#colors-and-styles
[20:31] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: so if you want to guarantee it has a certain display, you probably should address that in your style reset
[20:37] f4bfe7806ad6735f1dab2f9222fc539e: 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9, sure - but they should be a default, like for every other element. no?
[20:37] f4bfe7806ad6735f1dab2f9222fc539e: they = there
[20:40] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: thasmo that's up to the browser I believe
[20:40] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: it's just a matter of style
[20:40] f4bfe7806ad6735f1dab2f9222fc539e: 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9, hm that would be odd imo.
[20:40] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: not really, think about IE6
[20:40] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: inline-block didn't exist then
[20:41] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: so the spec for canvas can't dictate that it be inline-block, can it?
[20:41] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: html is separate from css, style is separate from markup, they should be completely decoupled..
[20:42] f4bfe7806ad6735f1dab2f9222fc539e: 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9, alright but why would a div then have 'block' as default?
[20:43] f4bfe7806ad6735f1dab2f9222fc539e: I mean, if IE renders 'canvas' as inline and chrome as 'block' and FX as 'inline-block' that just wouldn't be right? So I'm surprised if there was no specification for that.
[20:44] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: well IE won't render canvas as anything by default, it needs javascript shims for html5 elements and the canvas element specifically ..
[20:45] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: but basically it needs to work no matter what browsers do
[20:45] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: so it's not a spec for canvas, it's a spec for the canvas element
[20:45] 3fa179c2d34f53c18e7551ac493014d9: so it's not a spec for canvas, it's a spec for the canvas element
[20:46] f4bfe7")
