CONVERSATION:
[03:59] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Does http://canvex.lazyilluminati.com/misc/imagedata.html crash Opera 9.5? (I can only test via Opera Mini, which just says &quot;Internal server error&quot;, which sounds potentially worrying but not very informative)
[04:02] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: does Opera Mini handle events?
[04:03] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: and scripting?
[04:04] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: It seems to, as long as you don't use setInterval and don't expect it to wait for distant timeouts
[04:05] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (i.e. it can handle scripting and events and stuff while the page is loading, for some definition of 'loading' that I haven't quite worked out, though then it justs sends a static copy to your phone)
[04:05] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: *just
[04:07] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: so script runs at load time but not afterwards?
[04:08] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: Yes (as far as I can tell)
[04:09] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: (I'm playing with the Opera Mini simulator)
[04:09] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (since it basically opens the page in Opera on their servers, then at some point it decides it's got enough and transmits a non-interactive compressed snapshot, I think)
[04:09] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (Me too, since my real phone is far too rubbish :-) )
[04:11] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: I got it to run ~100 canvas tests in iframes on a single page, and that (eventually) worked correctly with all the scripting and loading and stuff, but it wouldn't let me correctly press the buttons to submit the test results, so I had to do that via a hard-coded timer :-(
[04:29] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: wonders if there could be getImageData(sx, sy, sw, sh, hires) where hires=true makes it return the full-resolution backing bitmap with width!=sw, otherwise it scales the bitmap down and returns with width==sw
[04:29] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: so people who don't know or don't care can just do getImageData(sx, sy, sw, sh) and get what looks like sensible pixels, whereas people who really want to do high-quality filters can set hires and take more care
[04:30] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (It's compatible with existing browsers and content, too...)
[04:31] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: putImageData would have to have the same flag
[04:31] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: (I'm not sure if it's possible to do that, though)
[04:32] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f79c: (I'm not sure if it's possible to do that, though)
[04:32] ab7faae5d7b250ea8606486575f8f")
