[12:51] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: chakie_work: About my QSocket TCP problem I got yesterday: I will modify the whole socket part to the way used in <a href="http://doc.trolltech.com/3.3/clientserver-example.html.">http://doc.trolltech.com/3.3/clientserver-example.html.</a> They are using QTextStream os(socket); and socket-&gt;canReadLine()
[12:51] e5c246c422bf5aeed2dab4c68c680e2b: you already said that... an hour ago
[12:51] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: My approach was QDataStream in(&amp;socket); and socket.writeBlock(block.data(), block.size());
[12:52] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: chakie_work: sorry My irc.cgi crashed..I have always to look for free irc.cgi gateways around in the web.
[12:52] e5c246c422bf5aeed2dab4c68c680e2b: why not use a real irc client?
[12:53] e5c246c422bf5aeed2dab4c68c680e2b: anyway, qtextstream is probably a better choice if the data is text anyway
[12:53] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: I think writeBlock maybe had a problem with &lt;CR&gt;, but anyway, readLine() seems to be the right way to send my string commands.
[12:53] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: Yes.
[12:54] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: chakie_work: I can't get IRC over the local transparent proxy here at my job.
[12:54] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: And besides forums, IRC is essential:)
[12:55] e5c246c422bf5aeed2dab4c68c680e2b: heh, ok
[12:55] e5c246c422bf5aeed2dab4c68c680e2b: works better now?
[12:57] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: canReadLine () returns true after &lt;CR&gt;?
[12:58] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: That would avoid the whole block counting for me. My first approach was counting the blocksize and compared it to bytes available..
[13:02] e5c246c422bf5aeed2dab4c68c680e2b: check the docs :)
[13:03] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: Yes, the say &quot;Returns TRUE if it's possible to read an entire line of text from this socket at this time;&quot;  I think they mean last character must be &lt;CR&gt;, I will try.
[12:53] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: Morning.  I have a Menu with exclusive toggle actions for setting the controler mode over TCP. With toggle signal I trigger a slot setMode.
[12:55] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: I think I have to use a different socket for the slot setMode
[12:55] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: I think I have to use a different socket for the slot setMode
[12:55] ff0a1b32b57b24924f2d5141321cb965: I think I have to use a different socket for the")
