[09:37] 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9: is confused by http://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-html/2008Dec/0088.html
[09:42] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9, yeah, I think Joshue is just confused
[09:43] 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9: f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220, the stuff about HTTP is what threw me. :)
[09:44] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: indeed
[09:44] 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9: I consider the off-screen model as being part of step 5
[09:45] 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9: the way ATs interact with web pages is, as Josh describes, something of a patchwork at the moment due to inadequate APIs, bugs in applications, dynamic content and so forth
[09:45] 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9: but the steps from 1-4 don't seem affected by that, afaict
[09:46] 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9: f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220, does the part Josh quoted from me make sense to you?
[09:47] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: This one isn't as clear as it could be &quot;The UA stores them in the relevant accessibility API properties.&quot;
[09:48] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: The UA stores the associations in an implementation specific way. It doesn't really matter how. The important part is that it reports those associations to the AT through the accessibility APIs
[09:52] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9,
[09:52] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: 1. The UA runs through the &lt;table&gt; once using the algorithm to find and store all of the associations between cells.
[09:52] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: 2. A user interacts with a cell via an AT.
[09:52] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: 3. The AT obtains the associations for the cell by querying the UA via the accessibility APIs
[09:53] 42e76c77af424a4350ab0e3e3f6f2ce9: f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220, yeah that makes sense
[09:53] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: I cut your original step 2 and 3 down to 1. The UA runs through the &lt;table&gt; once using the algorithm to find and store all of the associations between cells.
[09:53] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: 1. The UA runs through the &lt;table&gt; once using the algorithm to find and store all of the associations between cells.
[09:53] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a79")
