CONVERSATION:
[11:10] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: on the face of it, it doesn't seem too hard to replace the gc
[11:10] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: especially if you have boxing etc
[11:11] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: I think it might be tough to get a good generaly interface, becuase diff gc schemes require v. diff tagging and data representations, if you want to do them efficiently. (eg. refcounting has some nice optimizations, if you tell the gc things about lexical depth, etc)
[11:12] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: I hope it turns out that it will be easy to have them generic, though.
[11:12] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: hmm i see
[11:12] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: I haven't thought about it enough yet to have an opinion on how hard that will be.
[11:14] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: Right now, the thing is a pile of crap. One neat thing is, you can do this with it: cat program | lexer | parser | codegen
[11:15] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: that's neat
[11:15] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: i wish more things worked that way
[11:15] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: Thanks. I had to fight with myself hard to get it that way.
[11:18] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: don't back down on that
[11:18] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: No, it's been a mental fight to the death.
[11:20] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: Hmm, when ld says this,it's out of memory, right?
[11:20] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: ld: multiboot: Not enough room for program headers (allocated 4, need 5)
[11:21] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: no i don't think so
[11:21] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: i've seen that but don't quite know what caused it
[11:21] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: the same thing happened when I build OpenHackWare with gcc-3
[11:21] 2741b69c3b371bf320f870bfe5de76c7: with gcc-2.95 it didn't happen
[11:21] d6d06af1e06b96757067ab7bfc54b317: Oh - I have an idea. looks like they are using an explicit code segment size .. ld -T -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a -march=armv7-a")
