[02:22] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: Well, it's a nice way to organize and style it.
[02:22] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: I've updated the page using your suggestions.  I like it!
[02:24] c74f596e4fe95fc3bb8726dbde2031b0: :)
[02:25] c74f596e4fe95fc3bb8726dbde2031b0: I'm not sure &lt;a class=&quot;include&quot;&gt; can validly have text content.  The whole point is supposed to be for when you don't want there to be text content
[02:26] c74f596e4fe95fc3bb8726dbde2031b0: Also, I'm not sure if you can include an id that is not the actual element with the data you want...
[02:26] c74f596e4fe95fc3bb8726dbde2031b0: in this case, you actually want the &lt;a&gt; but are including the parent &lt;h1&gt;
[02:27] c74f596e4fe95fc3bb8726dbde2031b0: also, you now have still the two &lt;div&gt;s *and* have added a &lt;section&gt; inside... that's *more* cruft, not less :P
[02:27] c74f596e4fe95fc3bb8726dbde2031b0: Aside from that, looks pretty good
[02:32] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: Nothing changed with the &lt;div&gt;s and &lt;section.s
[02:33] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: c74f596e4fe95fc3bb8726dbde2031b0, well I am following the conventions, maybe not quite the way you intended, but they certainly work and they validate.
[02:35] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: The other thing is that, if I remove the text from that anchor, then the anchor is no longer accessible.
[02:35] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: Which is the point of anchors with hrefs.
[02:48] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: I swapped out the anchor with an object, since it seemed more apt.
[02:50] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: It's in the notes and issues &quot;Unlike the hyperlink pattern, the object is not believed to cause problems in assistive technology when fallback text is absent.&quot;
[02:51] 70bfd0ae2cfbf2da192bddd569cf6132: It would have been nice to use &lt;link&gt; but alas, no allowed.
