[05:21] 1e10d84b3917ae58049be95b0071cf7f: mikesmith 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e ping me if you have a moment. would like to discuss if it‚Äôs possible to add an exception for &lt;div&gt; to ‚ÄúIf a dl element contains non-whitespace text nodes, or elements other than dt and dd, then those elements or text nodes do not form part of any groups in that dl.‚Äù
[05:30] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: 1e10d84b3917ae58049be95b0071cf7f: not sure what you mean
[05:32] 1e10d84b3917ae58049be95b0071cf7f: 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: have had a couple of ppl mention &lt;dl&gt; is hard to use with CSS or JS because name-value associations don‚Äôt have a wrapper element.
[05:32] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: yeah, that's a bug in css
[05:32] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: we should fix it in css
[05:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: we could provide an array of DocumentFragment or something to make it easier in JS
[05:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: not clear what the use case is in JS
[05:33] 1e10d84b3917ae58049be95b0071cf7f: 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: aah. what about for JS? just implement the dl parsing algorithm in scripts?
[05:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: parsing?
[05:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: finding groups in JS is trivial
[05:33] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: you just collect nodes until you hit a dd then collect nodes until you hit a dt
[05:34] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and that's one group
[05:34] 1e10d84b3917ae58049be95b0071cf7f: well, the logic of dl (how multiple &lt;dt&gt; and &lt;dd&gt; are associated)
[05:34] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: then you repeat
[05:34] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: but depending on what the use cases are for manipulating &lt;dl&gt;s in script, we might be able to provide much better APIs for it
[05:34] 1e10d84b3917ae58049be95b0071cf7f: ok. need to follow up with that person coz not sure I understood fully (Japanese tweet, so brevity+language working against me :)
