[00:14] 28d34f2e053dee2c0e9399a7924cd978: Around?
[00:16] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: yes
[00:16] 28d34f2e053dee2c0e9399a7924cd978: nods, &quot;I'm curious as to your thoughts of today's events?&quot;
[00:16] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: svg nonsense?  much ado about nothing
[00:16] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: stvene dropped the ball.
[00:17] 28d34f2e053dee2c0e9399a7924cd978: Hm.
[00:19] 28d34f2e053dee2c0e9399a7924cd978: I admit to finding it more serious than that, both the actual dropping of the ball, and Rich's response.
[00:20] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: there was a long private discussion about the situation that steven and I were in on.  mark too I think.  tv raman.  all sorts of people
[00:20] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: it was very much &quot;w3c is fucked up how can we help fix this?&quot;
[00:21] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: Rick wanted to set up a con call so the parties could have a meeting of the minds.  I thought that was a fine idea as long as it shut up the &quot;we hate scoped attribute values&quot; people.  I know you are one of those people, but whatever.
[00:21] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: Rich often does not think before he types.
[00:21] 28d34f2e053dee2c0e9399a7924cd978: Well ... it certainly won't help the W3C with the way this is handled - nor is inviting, publically, a subset of people.
[00:21] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: that was the stupidest thing he has done in ages.
[00:22] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: people have side meetings all the time to work things out.  its smart.  making it a semi-official meeting was dumb
[00:22] 28d34f2e053dee2c0e9399a7924cd978: Yes, well, he might need to start doing that. I'm rather disappointed, I shall admit. As I mentioned before I started - time has been frightfully short for me, but while I don't begrudge you or Mark an invitation ... the phrasing was disgusting.
[00:23] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: quite
[00:23] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: this whole aria proposal has really irritated me.  and trying to appease these worthless html5 people makes me crazy
[00:23] 28d34f2e053dee2c0e9399a7924cd978: nods
[00:23] d656c4ec5f6dc8c4a13787760487cc0d: I think I'll just go ahead and close this thread.  I'm not going to bother with the discussion.  I'm not going to bother with the discussion.  I'm not going to bother with the discussion.  I'm not going to bother with the discussion.  I'm not going to bother with the discussion.  I'm not going to bother with the discussion.  I'm not going to bother with the discussion.  I'm")
