[20:14] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: Hi guys, I want to make an advent calendar where each door can be clicked on and opened up with animation
[20:14] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: What is the best way to go about doing this? Making animated gifs for tween?
[20:15] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: Or using entities and animating them?
[20:15] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: The latter I imagine would be much more difficult
[20:22] 9f873a67efcfe48cac10405dc48d2263: Well, it is a bit late for doing advent calendars :p But I think animated DIVs would be the most straight forward
[20:23] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: I know 9f873a67efcfe48cac10405dc48d2263, a late idea we wanna implement for next year :)
[20:23] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: Hence why I'm not shy to use HTML5
[20:23] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: So how would you go about doing that? Creating a DIV for the door and animating it with javascript?
[20:23] 9f873a67efcfe48cac10405dc48d2263: I'd probably use a div in a div with using a CSS animation to reveal the item undernieth
[20:23] 9f873a67efcfe48cac10405dc48d2263: underneath*
[20:24] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: ah ok
[20:24] 9f873a67efcfe48cac10405dc48d2263: That way the browser is taking care of all the hard work
[20:24] 9f873a67efcfe48cac10405dc48d2263: instead of you or javascript
[20:24] 738a5342e244e25b38d2cfc24bacc6fc: a DIV could sit atop the prize and clicking on it could make it slide away and then delete when it's 1px wide or whatever
