conv_id=2096 | raw="
CONVERSATION:
[04:01] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: Hixie: what would an implementation have to do to support the new semantic block-level elements?
[04:02] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: Hixie: would it be appropriate to give them default style of display: block, or no?
[04:02] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: Hixie: is it necessary to do some special rendering of &lt;h1&gt; - &lt;h6&gt; in the presence of sectioning elements?
[04:02] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: Hixie: I'm wondering because those seem like some of the least controversial additions in the spec, but I'm not sure what, if anything, implementations should do for those elements
[04:06] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c, display: block; for them would be very useful
[04:07] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: I'm not sure about heading rendering though
[04:07] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: I could see arguments either way - if they don't have display: block, content authors will be more likely to make documents that degrade gracefully by explicitly setting display: block
[04:07] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: I'm not sure what Hixie's intent was
[04:10] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: I think content authors will still set display: block for them to be compatible with legacy UAs during the transitional period until most UAs support them, though I think having the default has display: block; would be the most logical
[04:10] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: I think the bigger issue of backwards compatibility is the differences in parsing for known vs. unknown elements
[04:11] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: is there a parsing difference per spec?
[04:14] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: no, I meant the way in when legacy UAs will handle them as unknown elements and new UAs will parse them more sensibly
[04:14] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: although they're not in the parsing algorithm yet (last time I checked), I assume the sectioning elements will end up being parsed more like div
[10:02] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: Hixie, would it be possible for the spec to provide some sort of heuristic guidelines for programmatically determining when should be provided?  e.g. if you have &lt;h1&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;, it should be clear for a validator that the lack of alt text is an error.
[10:03] 65325d50b2e25aca54bc871b89758c9c: you could require alt in the spec, but I think that's a bit of a stretch
[10:03] f139aba52f9fa1394b4034a7954b2220: I think it's a bit of a stretch to require alt in the spec, but I think it's a bit of a stretch to require alt in the spec, but I think it's a bit of a stretch to require alt in the spec, but I think it's a bit of a stretch to require alt in the spec, but I think it's a bit of a stretch")
