[04:27] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: sayrer is gone, but for what it's worth, the way to get rid of things is twofold
[04:27] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: one way is to just ask for it to be removed. We've dropped quite a lot of stuff that way.
[04:27] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: Another way is that when the spec reaches near-zero major feedback, i do a run through and cut stuff out. we did this with wf2, for instance, and cut a bunch of crap out.
[04:28] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and another way, of course, is if no browsers implement it, it drops pretty much automatically..
[04:29] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: it should be noted that i recently proposed getting rid of &lt;event-source&gt;, and people screamed (with good arguments to back up their screams)
[04:29] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: i am also planning on dropping the &lt;dfn&gt; cross-ref crap
