[16:27] 1becfb88fded39b9b7b556e1ed9b611b: what ever dude! I can poke holes in fBSD/Linux/Solaris security...
[16:28] cfdfd0fdfc411ab448e8ee88c05ba352: Sure anyway, research show D-Link just had serious security issues
[16:28] cfdfd0fdfc411ab448e8ee88c05ba352: with not updating hen a bug was reported to them
[16:28] 1becfb88fded39b9b7b556e1ed9b611b: how many YEARS does it take sun patch a known security hole in the OS?
[16:28] cfdfd0fdfc411ab448e8ee88c05ba352: rather a year later when they went public
[16:28] cfdfd0fdfc411ab448e8ee88c05ba352: StoneNewt, because i say M$ has had troubles, i do not say all the rest hasn't
[16:29] cfdfd0fdfc411ab448e8ee88c05ba352: I just said that security issues aren't something, that often topples large companies, and that's not the case here
[16:29] cfdfd0fdfc411ab448e8ee88c05ba352: I'm not saying that D-Link is the only one that has security issues, but i'm saying that it's not the only one
[16:29] cfdfd0fdfc411ab448e8ee88c05ba352: I'm not saying that D-Link is the only one that has security issues, but i'm saying that it's not")
