CONVERSATION:
[02:47] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: hi ppl
[02:48] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: I uploaded my project (or whatever little is a start) to SourceForge (got a headache from trying to figure out Subversion, I used to use CVS long time ago but I dunno how well I did with SVN)
[02:50] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: there might be mistakes that could conflict with other javascript libs. If anyone wants to fix those, I'd be thankful for the help
[02:51] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: I chose the name Fiks.html for now (if anybody remembers, it's a script to make current browsers display HTML 5 correctly)
[02:52] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: I guess Fiks kind of works the best, and I omitted the O since I didn't have anywhere to put it, and Opera can be considered the least broken (it supports Web Forms 2.0 after all =) )
[02:53] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: if anybody wants to take a look, here's the SVN repo: http://fikshtml.svn.sourceforge.net/viewvc/fikshtml/
[02:59] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: I'm kinda getting the feeling I either get on when everyone's asleep, or whatwg might be the more appropriate room?
[03:02] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: i was responding to feedback on the list :-)
[03:02] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: looks cool
[03:03] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: you'll probably get more people on board once you've done a lot more work
[03:03] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: people seem to ignore people's ideas until those people have shown that they can actually do what they want to do :-)
[03:04] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: just look at the whatwg/html5 stuff, the amount of people who were interested in it has been directly proportional to how much work the people already involved had done so far
[03:05] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: well, my current todo list on the project isn't that much anyway. Just fix the display of new elements and changed elements
[03:05] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: and maybe the DOM
[03:05] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: cool
[03:06] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: but I don't want to reinvent the wheel with Web Forms 2.0 because it's already been done. A better solution would be to get it to integrate well with those existing projects
[03:06] d29ad639a6f502e926bdc7b458031ddd: I started my project becasue I haven't seen one like it already
[03:08] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: I'm not sure what you mean by "not seeing one like it already" but I'm pretty sure that's not the case. I've seen a lot of projects that are similar to yours, and I've seen a lot of projects that are similar to yours, and I've seen a lot of projects that are similar to yours, and I've seen a lot of projects that are similar to yours, and I've seen a lot of projects that are similar to yours, and I've seen a lot of projects that are similar to")
