[10:43] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: We do athentication with tomcat-users.xml. I want to have the users be in the database (postgressql). What should I be reading to learn about moving my user database into a real database?
[10:43] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: Ideally I would like users to be able to update their passwords, etc. Never done that sort of thing in tomcat until now.
[10:44] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: <a href="http://tomcat.apache.org/tomcat-4.0-doc/realm-howto.html">http://tomcat.apache.org/tomcat-4.0-doc/realm-howto.html</a>
[10:44] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: Is that a good explanation? Is there a better one?
[10:47] feab4dc99fda1f3538ce4795fe1ac92a: Voting: Are you really using Tomcat 4.0 ?
[10:48] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: wsmoak, got to ask someone...
[10:58] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: We still use 4.0.6 or something like that and I would rather not upgrade w/o a very good reason because we have so many good things working in this configuration...
[10:58] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: wsmoak, why do you ask?
[10:59] feab4dc99fda1f3538ce4795fe1ac92a: To make sure you're looking at the docs for the version you're actually using, rather than whatever you happened to find with a web search. :)
[10:59] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: Good point!
[11:00] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: wsmoak, have you used this sort of anthentication?
[11:01] feab4dc99fda1f3538ce4795fe1ac92a: No, I have a custom JAAS realm that talks to Kerberos.
[11:01] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: Can people change their passwords on the fly and that sort of thing?
[11:01] feab4dc99fda1f3538ce4795fe1ac92a: I think letting the users change their own passwords is another project entirely.
[11:02] feab4dc99fda1f3538ce4795fe1ac92a: That page explains how to get Tomcat talking to an existing database of users.
[11:02] feab4dc99fda1f3538ce4795fe1ac92a: How you maintain that database table is up to you.
[11:02] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: Hmm... JAAS sounds complex...
[11:03] feab4dc99fda1f3538ce4795fe1ac92a: Yes.  But that's not relevant to this discussion. :)
[11:04] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: I'm not sure I understand what you mean by "tomcat-users.xml". I'm not sure what you mean by "tomcat-users.xml" and "tomcat-users.xml" are you referring to the same thing?
[11:04] ee1fd9e44506800899a34b9410669b7c: I'm not sure what you mean by "tomcat-users.xml" and "tomcat-users.xml" are you referring to the same thing?
[11:04] ee1fd9e44")
