[21:10] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: wait, &lt;xmp&gt; is display:block? damnit i always forget that.
[21:26] 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: jgraham: welcome to pointless waste-of-time holy war
[21:27] 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: make sure your tabs are on the standard multiple-of-8-spaces so it works everywhere and move on with life
[21:47] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: anyone know about 'caller' being removed? do i just have to remove 'caller' from all my IDLs and then add this for document.all?:
[21:47] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: &lt;p&gt;In addition to the above, &lt;code&gt;HTMLAllCollection&lt;/code&gt; objects,
[21:47] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: in JavaScript, must be callable. Calling such an object must
[21:47] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: implicitly invoke the index getter with the same arguments.&lt;/p&gt;
[09:10] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: imho, the experimental prefixes should only be used with experimental features, not specced things.
[09:10] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: the problem is the csswg iterate for far too long instead of freezing fast like we do with the html spec
[09:11] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: they probably end up with more well-thought-out APIs eventually
[09:11] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: but in the meantime, we have to suffer through years of silliness :-)
[09:12] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: in other news, webkit has much prettier 'inset' and 'outset' border colours than firefox and opera
[09:12] 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: well, i've seen plenty of complaining on the lists about releasing APIs unprefixed too soon
[09:14] 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: with the way specs are developed these days, it might be worth clarifying somehow when the editor considers a spec stable enough for unprefixed implementations
[09:14] 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: seems like that's very fuzzy currently
[09:15] 06cb330920ae58e1614c9145d983b3d6: the websocket thread a week ago comes to mind
[09:15] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: websocket had the same problem with the old version of the spec
[09:15] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and it was fixed in the new version
[09:15] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: but it was not fixed in the new version of the spec
[09:15] 69b0d3dfe919a6b")
