CONVERSATION:
[22:06] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: what CSS spec would cover how CSS operates across frames (if it does at all), and is it implemented anywhere?
[22:06] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: anne, ^^
[22:06] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: (or anyone, really)
[22:07] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: so, if I have an SVG image in an object or iframe, can CSS in the HTML file be applied?
[22:09] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: No action across frames is defined anywhere.Wouldn't it be a security pb if it were?
[22:11] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: Transcluded content has to have its own style sheet (which may be the same, of course, but it needs to link to it by itself)
[22:12] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: (If you understand what &quot;it&quot; refers to. Sorry :-) )
[22:19] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: Actually, it's probably not a security problem. It just hasn't been urgent to define, because the browsers' handling of IMG and OBJECT is still nowhere near usable for anything but images :-(
[22:20] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: I think there is just one browser so far that is able to deal with IMG pointing to SVG...
[22:43] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65, you might find this interesting: http://www.schepers.cc/svg/blendups/embedding.html
[22:44] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: and we are working on an SVG Integration spec that defines and clarifies these scenarios
[22:45] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65, actually, both Opera and Safari work with the SVG in &lt;img&gt; and as CSS backgrounds, though Safari is buggy on both
[23:00] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: I don't see the bg in Opera.
[23:00] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: And why do you say the links should not work in IMG? That seems a bug to me.
[23:01] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: Also, when I click on the eyes, only the content of the OBJECT is replaces, not the whole page. Why is that? That seems wrong, too.
[23:03] bddfdb28870c5800d938fa0993c46d65: Animation in a bg should run, just as in a foreground image. What should keep them from doing so? (Assuming the media is capable of dynamic rendering, of course. E.g., paper isn't.)
[22:29] 227a9a17d1db3f8e5c71a150345fb2a6: I think it's a security problem. I don't think it's a bug. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I think it's a security problem. I")
