CONVERSATION:
[02:21] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: Hey, I have a question about XHTML5: why do you even support XHTML5 if you're not going to define a DTD for it? No named entities work in XHTML5 because there's no SYSTEM in the DOCTYPE.
[02:22] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: there needs to be a system for XHTML5 like &lt;!DOCTYPE html SYSTEM &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/html5/DTD/html5.dtd&quot;&gt;
[02:22] a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: Is there only any point in it if it has named entities?
[02:23] a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: Bear in mind parsers aren't required to read the DTD
[02:23] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: it makes XHTML5 useless/dangerous as most people will assume they can use named entities like &amp;nbsp;
[02:23] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: I know, but at least firefox does
[02:23] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: and chrome ignore it
[02:23] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: ignores*
[02:24] a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: People can't safely use them even if it does have one for the above reason. It seems safer for it to always be a fatal error and make sure it's consistent.
[02:25] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: so you're saying that XHTML5 users shouldn't be allowed to enjoy the pre-defined named entities in HTML5?
[02:26] a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: They can't ever rely upon them even if there is an external DTD
[02:26] a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: So, yes, it seems safer to not allow them to,
[02:26] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: that's not the point
[02:26] a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: And when you should probably be using a serializer to ensure your output well-formed, you shouldn't manually be dealing with entities anyway‚
[02:26] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea06b56554: I'm not sure what you mean by that
[02:26] 5b9cb20d2f71fee5f77d39d8e5b3129c: a11aabeeceeae6b8cb5d12ea")
