CONVERSATION:
[10:08] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: can anyone point me to an example of an HTML5 canvas rectangle drawn with a border that uses an image instead of a color?
[10:20] 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: do you know specific dimensions of the rectangle?
[10:21] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: yes. I drew it. Here's what I found works: context.style = &quot;border-image: url(image.gif) 100%;&quot;; then doing a strokeRect
[10:22] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: but i'm not sure that it's the right way to go
[10:23] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: also, i would have expected an animated image to result in an animated border
[10:23] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: which is disappointing
[10:25] 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: here is your literal answer http://i.imgur.com/tZ5ZH.png
[10:25] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: i was looking for an implementation example. I thought maybe I was doing it wrong, resulting in the border not being animated :(
[10:26] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: it is nifty
[10:28] 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: add some JS and animate it?
[10:29] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: it doesnt even load the image into the border (just gives a black border). animating a border with say... a marquee (select tool moving dashed line), would be a little too intensive for js
[10:35] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: context.createPattern(imageObj,'repeat') &lt;-- the pattern can be fed as a strokestyle, so now I have the image loading as a border, but it isn't animated (although the source image is an animated gif)
[10:36] 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: browser?
[10:36] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: chrome
[10:37] baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: v 12.0.1
[10:38] 97f8fe2ffd67e0999af7060e16c7ad77: baab1d24fd97b3aecdcb2c1a98bc4881: I'm not sure if this is the right way to go, but I'm not sure if it's the right way to go either. I'm not sure if it's the right way to go, but I'm not sure if it's the right way to go either.
[10:39] ba")
