CONVERSATION:
[22:51] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: that's what i had originally (error then close) but people complained that that made it unnecessarily hard to know whether to try to reconnect
[22:52] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: whatwg.org is the latest one
[22:52] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: personally i recommend the complete.html file since it has the api and the protocol all together in done doc with cross-references
[22:53] bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: are there emails about the error and close in some mailing list?
[22:55] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: i don't recall if it was mailing list feedback or irc feedback
[22:58] bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: why reconnecting is hard?
[22:58] bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: er, to know whether to reconnect
[22:59] bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: and how does wasClean help with that
[23:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: with wasClean you just do if (!event.wasClean) { reconnect() } else { doNormalShutdown(); }
[23:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: without it you have to set a flag in the error handler and check the flag in the close handler
[23:01] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: it's certainly not a big effort
[23:02] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: but it seems more than necessary, especially if the only reason to avoid it is to make implementation life easier
[23:02] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: the order of priorities goes: users &gt; authors &gt; implementors &gt; spec writers
[23:02] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: so authors basically always get their way unless the pain on implementors is inordinate
[23:03] bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: without wasClean you reconnect in the error handler
[23:03] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and the else?
[23:03] bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: ah, right
[23:03] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and the else is the close handler
[23:03] bb21c722adad611b63dfb48ec99e8350: and the else is the close handler
[23:03] 69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e: and the else is the close handler
[23:03] bb21")
