[23:10] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: have you guys implemented border-break or background-break yet
[23:11] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c, we've implemented background-break for ages as -moz-background-inline-policy, but for inlines only
[23:11] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: background-break seems problematic for columns broken across pages
[23:11] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: based on hixie's proposal for years ago
[23:11] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: from
[23:11] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: for multicols broken across pages you have two types of breaks
[23:11] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: and it seems like a valid use case to want to do e.g., each-box but on the pages
[23:11] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: and not on the cols
[23:12] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: or continuous but on the pages and not the cols
[23:13] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: what about border-break? implemented that?
[23:15] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: i don't really understand how to implement border-break on inlines if it has to be included in the line breaking algorithm
[23:15] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: it gets completely insane
[23:15] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: like if the border that only appears if you break early is thicker than the real edge border
[23:15] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: you could end up thinking you don't fit in the middle, but do fit if you keep going to the end
[23:16] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c, is it worse than borders already are?
[23:16] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: yes
[23:16] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: because they're pretty bad even without border-break
[23:16] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: because there's now an unpredictable border
[23:16] 104bc19e5513cba4eba2d18c7a704a01: and it's not just a border
[23:16] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: it's a border that's not just a border
[23:16] cd3e478e1fb92aef95961d138529f52c: it's a border that's not just a border
[23:16] cd3e478")
